          "channelId": "1300025221834739744",
          "channelName": "💬-coders",
          "summary": "The channel discussed two main technical topics. First, tcgkylee inquired about connecting to LMstudio and quickly resolved it independently by finding the official plugin at github.com/elizaOS/eliza/tree/develop/plugins/plugin-lmstudio. The more substantial discussion came from paulf76, who shared a newly developed trading agent plugin called cabal-hunter. The plugin addresses a critical blind spot in trading agents: identifying malicious actors and risky token structures that price/volume data alone cannot detect. The plugin performs on-chain wallet graph analysis to trace holder clusters, funding sources, bundled buyers, serial-rug deployers, and honeypot LPs (including freeze authority and token-2022 traps). It provides a verdict that agents can use to gate buy decisions. The plugin is available via npm as elizaos-plugin-cabal-hunter with the first 100 scans free, requiring approximately 3 lines of code to integrate. The developer is actively seeking feedback from other trading agent operators on additional signals to incorporate before buy decisions.",
